@startuml kgbench-token-attribution
!include _standard-style.puml

title kgbench — how a cell's token count is established

top to bottom direction

component "claude cell" <<agent>> as CLAUDE
component "copilot cell" <<agent>> as COPILOT
component "opencode cell" <<agent>> as OPENCODE

component "stream-json\nresult event" <<core>> as SJ
component "x-task-id header\nper request" <<core>> as HDR
component "stop-adapter\ncopadt / opcadt" <<core>> as ADAPT

component "rapid-llm-proxy\n:12435" <<infra>> as PROXY
database "token_usage\nrows" <<storage>> as DB

component "resolveCellTokens()" <<core>> as RES
component "aggregateByTaskId()\nexact: tagged as this cell" <<core>> as BYID
component "aggregateByWindow()\ninferred: ran while it ran" <<core>> as BYWIN

component "row.token_source" <<util>> as SRC

CLAUDE DATA_LINE SJ : first-party,\nexact
CLAUDE SYNC_LINE HDR
HDR SYNC_LINE PROXY

COPILOT SYNC_LINE PROXY
OPENCODE SYNC_LINE PROXY
COPILOT DATA_LINE ADAPT : session id\nthe harness\nnever learns
OPENCODE DATA_LINE ADAPT
ADAPT DATA_LINE DB
PROXY DATA_LINE DB

SJ DATA_LINE RES
RES CONTROL_LINE BYID
BYID OPTIONAL_LINE BYWIN : no rows\nfor this task_id
BYID DATA_LINE DB
BYWIN DATA_LINE DB
RES DATA_LINE SRC

note right of SRC
  stream-json      first-party, exact
  proxy-db-taskid  tagged, exact
  proxy-db-window  time join, weaker
  unmeasured       null, never 0
end note

note right of BYWIN
  Sound only because cells run
  serially and the window is
  scoped to one agent. More than
  one session inside the window
  sets token_ambiguous.
end note

note bottom of ADAPT
  Rows can land a MINUTE after the
  cell ends, so resolution must be
  re-runnable offline
  (kgbench-backfill-tokens.mjs).
end note

@enduml
